PATCH 171: FUN_0000_4846 (asm 0x4846) -- a CS-relative static method dispatch on the display-
list paint path (459a -> 206f -> 209e -> 4846), the same class as the 0x8342 voxel dispatch
(patch 159): Ghidra drops the `2e` CS-override prefix.  asm `mov bx,[DGROUP:0x7a40]; call word
CS:[bx+0x4850]` -- bx = the element state selector word[DGROUP:0x7a40]; the near-call target is
word at the STATIC table CS:0x4850 (CS=0 -> linear 0x4850 in the base-0 code image; table[0] =
0x4854 = FUN_0000_4854).  Ghidra emitted `*(int*)(DAT_2000_3a40 + 0x4850)` (near-offset used as
host ptr) -> the SIGSEGV at FUN_0000_4846 (fault 0x4850).  Rebased: bx from DGROUP, the table
read from g_mem+0 (CS=0).  Behaviour-neutral for verify (paint path, unreached by the 19 flows).

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -13325,7 +13325,16 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_4846(void)
 
 {
-  (*(code *)fist_icall_near(0x0u,(uint16_t)(*(undefined2 *)(DAT_2000_3a40 + 0x4850))))();
+  /* PATCH 171 (asm 0x4846): a CS-relative static dispatch (same class as the 0x8342 voxel dispatch,
+     patch 159 -- Ghidra drops the `2e` CS prefix).  asm `mov bx,[DGROUP:0x7a40]; call word CS:[bx+
+     0x4850]` -- bx = word[DGROUP:0x7a40] (the element state selector), the target is word at the
+     STATIC table CS:0x4850 (CS=0 -> linear 0x4850 in the base-0 code image; table[0]=0x4854=FUN_0000
+     _4854).  Ghidra rendered it `*(int*)(DAT_2000_3a40 + 0x4850)` = a wild host deref (SIGSEGV at
+     4846, fault 0x4850; paint path 459a->206f->209e->4846).  Rebase: bx from DGROUP, the table read
+     from g_mem+0 (CS=0), both 16-bit. */
+  uint16_t bx = *(uint16_t *)(g_mem + 0x1c000 + 0x7a40);
+  uint16_t tgt = *(uint16_t *)(g_mem + (uint16_t)(bx + 0x4850));
+  (*(code *)fist_icall_near(0x0u,tgt))();
   return;
 }
 
